---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — EyesRhythm"
  description="EyesRhythm is offline after a one-time license activation. Camera frames never leave the machine. No accounts, no cloud, no analytics."
>
  <main id="main" class="section" style="background:#fff;padding-bottom:96px">
    <article class="wrap legal">
      <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker__dot"></span>Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="display">On-device and private.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        EyesRhythm is meant to sit next to your work, not on someone else’s
        server. This page states that plainly.
      </p>

      <h2>What never leaves the machine</h2>
      <p>
        After this copy is activated, no internet is required for normal use.
        There is no account, no login, no cloud, and no analytics. Camera
        frames are processed on this computer only, in real time. Video is not
        recorded for upload, not stored as a film of your face, and not shared.
      </p>

      <h2>License activation (first launch only)</h2>
      <p>
        A paid copy is sold through Lemon Squeezy. They take payment, email a
        unique license key to the address you give at checkout, and store
        activations. On first launch the app asks for that key and, with your
        permission and an internet connection, sends the key plus a hashed
        machine identifier to Lemon Squeezy so this computer can run the copy
        you bought. That is the only time EyesRhythm talks to the internet.
        Blink metrics and camera frames are never part of that request.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each purchase is one operating system (macOS or Windows) on one
        computer. A Mac key will not activate a Windows copy, and the reverse
        is also true.
      </p>

      <h2>What may be kept locally</h2>
      <p>
        What is kept, if anything, is yours: today’s blink and screen-time
        totals, preferences, and optional on-device history for your own
        reports. That data stays in a folder on the computer and resets or
        remains there according to the app. It is not sent to us or to anyone
        else.
      </p>
      <p>
        On macOS and Windows the local folder is typically under your home
        directory as <code>.eyerhythm_blinkcounter</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing the app</h2>
      <p>
        When a copy is issued, you receive the installer for the OS you paid
        for. The recipient runs it locally. After activation there is no
        “phone home.” This website does not host installers.
      </p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a static page. It does not set cookies, does not load
        analytics, and does not call third-party scripts. “Get a copy” sends
        you to Lemon Squeezy’s checkout (a different site) to pay. We never
        see card numbers.
      </p>

      <h2>Not a medical device</h2>
      <p>
        EyesRhythm is a wellness companion. It has not been cleared or approved
        by the FDA or any other regulator. It is not intended to diagnose,
        treat, cure, or prevent disease. ORI is a cadence score you can act on —
        not a diagnosis. If you have an ocular surface disorder, a change in
        vision, or persistent discomfort, consult a licensed eye-care
        professional.
      </p>

      <p><a href="/#privacy">Back to the site</a></p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .legal p {
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }

  code {
    font-size: 0.88em;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
</style>
